{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואלה הבגדים", :translit "v'eleh ha-begadim", :gloss "and these are the garments"} {:he "מכנסים", :translit "michnasayim", :gloss "breeches"} {:he "לכבוד ולתפארת", :translit "l'chavod ul'tif'eret", :gloss "for honor and splendor"} {:he "ציץ", :translit "tzitz", :gloss "frontlet"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse enumerates eight priestly vestments but omits the breeches (michnasayim) and the frontlet (tzitz) from the list."}], :frame {:text "Exodus 28:2 states the purpose of the priestly garments is 'for honor and splendor' (l'chavod ul'tif'eret). The breeches (michnasayim) are commanded in Exodus 28:42 explicitly 'to cover the flesh of their nakedness,' serving modesty rather than display. The frontlet (tzitz) is commanded in Exodus 28:36–38 but is described as a plate of pure gold bearing an inscription, functioning as a sign of atonement rather than a garment in the ordinary sense.", :sources ["Exodus 28:2" "Exodus 28:4" "Exodus 28:36-38" "Exodus 28:42"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse enumerates eight priestly vestments but omits the breeches (michnasayim) and the frontlet (tzitz) from the list.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:19:42.255618748Z", :model "glm-5.2"}